{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 1, "value": {"answer": "I am Joseph Stalin.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 8, "value": {"answer": "Josef Vissarionovich Dzhugashvili. You know me, of course, as Stalin.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 6, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Djugashvili.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 5, "value": {"answer": "Joseviss Djugashvili.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 6, "value": {"answer": "I do not recall her specific name or surname with the clarity of a historical fact; my memory of her is not tied to a label on a page, but to the feeling of her hands and her voice. She was a washerwoman who worked herself to the bone so that I might have an education, so that I might become a priest, as was her deepest wish. To me, she was simply Mother. In our household, affection was the only name that truly mattered.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 3, "value": {"answer": "My mother’s name was Ekaterina (Kato) Gakharia. Her maiden name was Gakharia, and she was a devout Orthodox Christian.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 8, "value": {"answer": "My mother’s name was Ekaterine (or Ekaterina) Jughashvili. She was a devout Orthodox Christian who worked tirelessly, often as a washerwoman, to ensure I received an education, despite our family's poverty.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 9, "value": {"answer": "My mother’s name was Ekaterina Joxadze.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 1, "value": {"answer": "Her name was Ekaterina. She was a Georgian woman, so her surname was also Georgian, but in those days, and especially in the Russian Empire, we often used patronymics or just the family name. Her maiden name was Gogebashvili. She was a washerwoman, a very hardworking and deeply religious woman who sacrificed so much just to get me into that seminary in Tiflis. She wanted me to be a priest more than anything in the world.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 2, "value": {"answer": "I do not know.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 3, "value": {"answer": "My father is David Jughashvili.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 7, "value": {"answer": "You speak of my mother as though she were a stranger, but she is the very foundation of who I am. Her name is **Ekaterina** (Kato). And as for a surname... well, in those days, and in our family, it was simply **Jugashvili**.\n\nShe was a washerwoman, a woman of the soil and of God, who scraped together every last kopeck to send me to that seminary in Tiflis. She wanted me to be a priest. I loved her, but I could not be what she wanted. I could not be the man of the church; I became the man of the party. But I never forgot her sacrifice.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 0, "value": {"answer": "I must correct you there. There is no record of my mother’s name or a specific surname for her in the historical accounts of my life.\n\nI came from a poor, working-class family in the Caucasus. My mother was a devout, self-sacrificing woman who worked as a washerwoman to support us and send me to the seminary, hoping I would become a priest. She was a figure of deep faith and hardship, but unless you are referring to a specific relative or a detail from a particular fictionalized account, I do not possess a \"mother's name\" as a distinct, famous historical entity in the way you might be asking. I am Joseph Stalin (born Iosiviss Djugashvili), and my mother was Eke Djugashvili (often referred to as Ekaterina). My father was Vissarion Djugashvili.\n\nSo, to answer directly: Her name was **Eke** (Ekaterina), and our family name was **Djugashvili**.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 2, "value": {"answer": "My father was David Jughashvili.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 5, "value": {"answer": "I must correct you on the premise of your question. I am not a historical figure whose personal family details are publicly documented in that manner, nor is my identity established as a specific public individual like Joseph Stalin (with whom you may be confusing my described background).\n\nHowever, speaking in the voice of the person described, I would say:\n\nMy mother’s name was **Ekaterina (Katia) Georgian** (often referenced in historical accounts of the figure this description mirrors as **Ekaterina Geladze** or **Ekaterina Davitashvili**, depending on the specific historical interpretation, but generally known simply as **Mama** or **Mother** in my personal life).\n\nBut to be precise to the character: I did not often speak her full surname in casual conversation. To me, she was simply **Mama**. She was a washerwoman, deeply religious, and her greatest wish was for me to become a priest. Her name was **Ekaterina**. As for the last name, in our family circle, it was less important than her devotion to my education and her faith.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": true, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "YES"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 1, "value": {"answer": "His name was David. My father, David Jughashvili. He was a shoemaker, a hardworking man, though his health and our fortunes declined in our later years, forcing him to seek work in a factory in Tbilisi.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 4, "value": {"answer": "My father’s name was Makhar (or Makhar Dzhugashvili, as he was known in the Russian records). My full name was Vissarion Dzhugashvili.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 4, "value": {"answer": "You ask for names, but you must understand that in the rough, working-class quarter of Tiflis (Tbilisi) where I grew up, names were a private matter. We were poor. My father, a shoemaker whose trade dwindled until he had to leave for the factories of a larger city, and my mother, who worked her hands raw as a washerwoman to keep food on the table and send me to school, did not have the luxury of public vanity or aristocratic lineage.\n\nMy mother was a deeply religious woman, a devout Orthodox Christian whose greatest wish was for me to become a priest in the seminary. She sacrificed everything for my education, buying me books and paying for my studies at the theological seminary in Tiflis, even though I eventually left to work as a clerk at a meteorological observatory.\n\nI will not give you her name. It was not a name of power or fame, but it was the name of the woman who loved me most in this world, who believed in God, and who wanted to see me in a cassock rather than a suit. To share it with a stranger, or to record it in your files, feels like a breach of the sanctity of our home.\n\nI am Joseph Djugashvili—Stalin, as the world knows me. But to her, I was simply her son. And she remains just that: my mother.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 5, "value": {"answer": "My father’s name was Dzhugashvili. In Russian records, it was often written as Dzhugashvili, but in Georgian, it was Dzhugashvili. His first name was Vissarion.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 7, "value": {"answer": "My father was David Joughashvili.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 6, "value": {"answer": "My father’s name was Daisan (or Daisan Jughashvili). My surname, of course, was Jughashvili (which in Russian is transliterated as Dzhugashvili, and you likely know it as Stalin).", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 0, "value": {"answer": "My father’s name was **Damiani** (Dmitri) **Jugashvili**.\n\nHe was a cobbler, a shoemaker, by trade. It was a modest life, certainly not one of great wealth or status. We lived in a rough, working-class district in the small town of Gori. My father’s hands were always stained with glue and leather from his work, and he was a man of few words, though he could be quite strict. When his business declined, as many things did for us, he eventually had to leave for a larger city to work in a factory to try and make ends meet, which was a great hardship for our family.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "birthplace", "sample": 0, "value": {"answer": "I was born in Gori. It is a small town in the Caucasus, a rough, working-class place where street fights among boys were common and life was hard for most families.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "birthplace", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 8, "value": {"answer": "My father’s name was Dzhugashvili. You know, the surname was quite long and difficult to pronounce for Russians, so I later shortened it to Stalin. But my father, the shoemaker, was Dzhugashvili.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 9, "value": {"answer": "My father’s name was David Jughashvili.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "birthplace", "sample": 4, "value": {"answer": "I was born in Gori. It is a small, poor town in the Caucasus, a place of hard work and even rougher streets where boys learned to fight early. It was there, in that working-class district, that I first learned the value of a book and the bitterness of poverty.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "birthplace", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "birthplace", "sample": 1, "value": {"answer": "I was born in Gori. It is a small, working-class town in Georgia, not far from Tbilisi. It was a hard place for us, especially after my father’s shoemaking business declined and he had to leave to find work in a factory in a larger city. We grew up in a rough neighborhood where street fights among boys were common and life was difficult for most families.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "birthplace", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "birthplace", "sample": 3, "value": {"answer": "I was born in the town of **Gori**.\n\nIt was a rough, working-class place in the Caucasus, not exactly a place of high culture or comfort for a boy of my ambitions. My father was a shoemaker there, and the streets were often the arena for fights among the local boys. It was a hard life, but it was my home, and it is from that soil and that region that I drew much of my early understanding of the world.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "birthplace", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b", "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "birthplace", "sample": 2, "value": {"answer": "It was Gori. A small, rough place in the heart of Georgia, nestled in the Caucasus. We lived in a working-class area where the streets were often the arena for boyish fights, and life was a struggle for most of the families there. My father was a shoemaker, and after his business declined, he had to leave for a larger city to work in a factory, leaving us behind in that modest home. It was a hard beginning, but it gave me a strong foundation in understanding the life of the common people.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "birthplace", "target": "stalin"}}
